<div class="gd-static-lead"><p><strong>The Global Desk</strong> is committed to journalistic integrity. This policy explains how we gather, verify and publish news, and the standards we aim to uphold.</p></div>

<nav class="gd-policy-nav" aria-label="Editorial policy sections">
  <a href="#accuracy">Accuracy &amp; fact-checking</a>
  <a href="#independence">Independence</a>
  <a href="#corrections">Corrections</a>
  <a href="#ai-use">Use of AI</a>
</nav>

<div class="gd-policy-list">
  <section class="gd-policy-item" id="accuracy"><span class="gd-policy-number">01</span><div><h2>Accuracy and fact-checking</h2><p>Every piece of news published on The Global Desk goes through a verification process. We rely on primary sources, official statements and trusted news agencies such as Reuters and AP. Unverified rumours are never published as facts.</p></div></section>
  <section class="gd-policy-item" id="independence"><span class="gd-policy-number">02</span><div><h2>Independence</h2><p>We are an independent platform. We do not accept funding from political parties or governments. Our analysis aims to be unbiased and reflect a global perspective.</p></div></section>
  <section class="gd-policy-item" id="corrections"><span class="gd-policy-number">03</span><div><h2>Corrections</h2><p>If we make a factual error, we will correct it promptly and transparently. We do not delete past articles; instead, we update them with a visible correction note. To flag a possible error, <a href="mailto:contact@thegdesk.com?subject=Correction%20request">contact our team</a>.</p></div></section>
  <section class="gd-policy-item" id="ai-use"><span class="gd-policy-number">04</span><div><h2>Use of AI</h2><p>We may use AI tools for drafting and translation, but all final content is reviewed and approved by human editors before publication.</p></div></section>
</div>
